                                "sense_id": "6af1df40-9067-3edd-9270-3c0b793259e9",
                                "text": "\"Country?\" replied Cuddie; \"ou, the country's weel eneugh, and it werena that dour deevil, Calver'se, ( they ca' him Dundee now) that's stirring about yet in the Highlands, they say, with a' the Donalds, and Duncans, and Dugalds, that ever wore bottomless breeks, driving about wi' him, to set things asteer again, - - -"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d24ee39-effb-416f-9052-3fc78c4077ec",
                                "sense_id": "6af1df40-9067-3edd-9270-3c0b793259e9",
                                "text": "One aim of the move [from Nine Elms] had been to speed up the overhaul of the company's locomotive stock and to reduce costs with more efficient workshop facilities, in what Dugald Drummond claimed to be \"the most complete and up-to-date works owned by any railway company\"."
                            }
